  "chapter": 695,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 79 Chapter 695\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 2014, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the administrative code of the city of New York,\n        the emergency tenant protection act  of  nineteen  seventy-four,\n        the  emergency  housing  rent  control law and the real property\n        law, in relation to prohibiting charges for legal fees\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill helps protect renters from legal fees assessed by  landlords\nabove and beyond what tenants already pay in rent. The bill prohibits an\nowner,  lessor  or  agent from assessing a lessee any fee, surcharge, or\nother charges for legal services in connection  with  the  operation  or\nrental of a residential unit, unless such legal fees were awarded pursu-\nant  to a court order. The bill applies to all rental housing regardless\nof regulatory status, and further provides that the  restriction  cannot\nbe waived by agreement or assessment.\n \n  I  am  supportive of the bill and believe that it will protect tenants\nfrom increasingly expensive and unwarranted  fees.  I  have  reached  an\nagreement with the legislature to make an amendment to the bill to clar-\nify  that  cooperative  housing  corporations  can  impose legal fees on\nshareholders,  while  simultaneously  clarifying  that  the  shareholder\ncannot  impose the fees on a tenant or subtenant living in a cooperative\nhousing unit.\n \n  With these changes, I am pleased to sign  this  piece  of  legislation\ninto law.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2021
 },
